{"type": "answer", "t": "2026-11-16T12:29:48-05:00", "question_id": "q1794849674", "question": "4♦h (onto 3♦) was available: missed, or held back?", "game": "K473-20261116-115506-0959", "n": 40, "text": "Held back: if the 3♣ becomes playable, it can be played on the 4♦. At this point in the game, the potential for a future play of 3♣ outweighs the relatively benign current moves of 4♦ to home. Also, as a general rule, I try not to play a card to home if it is more than two ranks higher than the lowest card of the opposite color currently played to a home pile. I'm already one play ahead to the home pile than I'd like to be (3♦) since the A♣ hasn't been played yet (which essentially means that the current lowest black card play to a home pile is the 0♣).", "via": "panel"}
